# On layouts/path-field.jsonc a Federation destroyer at (1500, 2000) is ordered to (2500, 2000), straight across an
# asteroid field at (2000, 2000). The game's path planner costs the field as an impassable square of half the belt distance
# 150 x 0.5 = 75 around its position (the cells it touches reach 50 further) inside a ring of three times the default cost,
# so the ship does not fly the straight line: its path bends around the square, and the dumps while it passes show its
# distance from the line z = 2000 beyond the square's reach (more than 125). Across open space the same order is the
# straight line.
# Dumps: "start" (0.2 s) shows the ship at its place with move=none; "driving" (3 s) shows it on its way with
# move=2500.00,-2000.00; "pass1" to "pass3" (20, 25, and 30 s) show it passing the field 190 off the line z = -2000
# (the dump's pos= z is the layout z mirrored): at x 2017 in "pass3" its z is -1810.58, and it is never nearer than 125
# to the line between x 1925 and 2075. The fast-forward runs the world, undrawn, until the order ends: "arrived" shows it
# within 40 of the point with move=none.
# Run it with --layout layouts/path-field.jsonc; the layout's header comment has the whole command.
# The point is in the frame of the dump's pos= field, whose z is the layout z mirrored.
wait 0.2
dump start
select Mover
wait 0.3
move 2500 -2000
wait 2.5
dump driving
wait 17
dump pass1
wait 5
dump pass2
wait 5
dump pass3
fast-forward until Mover move = none max 60
dump arrived
wait 0.1
shot arrived Mover
